Package: agentreliabilityeb
Title: Empirical-Bayes Reliability Testing for Stochastic AI-Agent Tasks
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Shikhar", "Sehgal", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Course project (STAT 27855). Compares oracle, nonparametric and
    Beta-binomial empirical-Bayes local false discovery rates, an unpooled Beta(1,1)
    baseline, and exact binomial tests with BH/BY for deciding which benchmark tasks
    meet a reliability threshold, and quantifies non-identification of the lfdr
    when each task has only a few binary runs. Analysis repository, not an
    installable package: functions are sourced via R/load.R.
License: MIT
Depends: R (>= 4.3)
Imports: lpSolve, jsonlite, knitr, ggplot2
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Encoding: UTF-8
